<h1>From an app to a Worker</h1>
<p class="lead">Five steps. The first is done once per Soli version; the others are your
everyday loop.</p>

<ol class="steps">
  <li>
    <h2>Build the edge runtime</h2>
    <p>In the Soli source tree: the release archives carry <code>soli</code> alone. It needs the
       wasm32 target and the wasm-bindgen CLI at the version <code>edge/Cargo.toml</code> pins;
       the script says which if they are missing.</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version 0.2.126 --locked
./scripts/build-edge.sh                      # → target/edge
export SOLI_EDGE_RUNTIME=~/soli/target/edge  # where soli edge finds it</code></pre>
  </li>
  <li>
    <h2>Start an app for Workers</h2>
<pre><code class="language-bash">soli new my_app --edge
cd my_app</code></pre>
    <p>The usual application, set up to deploy as a Worker:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>wrangler.toml</code> beside <code>app/</code>: models on D1, sessions in an encrypted
          cookie, CSRF tokens required, and the R2, Images, Durable Objects, Queues and Hyperdrive
          blocks ready to uncomment. Every build copies it in: commit it.</li>
      <li><code>.env</code>, for <code>soli serve</code> on your machine: the same models on SQLite
          (D1 is SQLite) and the same cookie sessions.</li>
      <li><code>.dev.vars</code>, the session secret for local runs; never committed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>An app you already have needs nothing but a <code>wrangler.toml</code> next to
       <code>app/</code>: <code>app/</code>, <code>config/</code> and <code>lib/</code> go into the
       Worker, <code>public/</code> becomes its static assets, <code>.env</code> stays out.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <h2>Develop on workerd</h2>
<pre><code class="language-bash">soli edge dev                    # http://localhost:8787</code></pre>
    <p>That is Cloudflare's own runtime, locally: what works here works deployed. It repackages
       the app on every change under <code>app/</code>, <code>config/</code>, <code>lib/</code> or
       <code>public/</code>, and wrangler reloads the page. D1, R2, Queues and the Durable Objects
       are local copies, in <code>dist/edge/.wrangler/state</code>.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <h2>Wire the services</h2>
    <p>Create what the app uses, put the id or name Wrangler prints in its
       <code>wrangler.toml</code> block, and uncomment it. Each one is detailed
       <a href="/#gates-title">on the home page</a>.</p>
    <table class="board wiring">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">For</th><th scope="col">Create it</th><th scope="col">Then</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="code"><a href="/#sqlite">D1</a></td>
          <td><code>npx wrangler d1 create my_app-db</code></td>
          <td>its <code>database_id</code> in <code>[[d1_databases]]</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="code"><a href="/#postgres">Postgres</a></td>
          <td><code>npx wrangler hyperdrive create my-db --connection-string="postgres://…"</code></td>
          <td><code>[[hyperdrive]]</code>, <code>nodejs_compat</code>, <code>SOLI_DB_ADAPTER = "postgres"</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="code"><a href="/#r2">R2</a></td>
          <td><code>npx wrangler r2 bucket create my_app-files</code></td>
          <td><code>[[r2_buckets]]</code>, and <code>"service": "r2"</code> on the attachment</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="code"><a href="/#images">Images</a></td>
          <td>nothing to create</td>
          <td><code>[images]</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="code"><a href="/#queues">Queues</a></td>
          <td><code>npx wrangler queues create my_app-jobs</code></td>
          <td><code>[[queues.producers]]</code> and <code>[[queues.consumers]]</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="code"><a href="/#sqlite">Durable Objects</a></td>
          <td>nothing to create: an object exists once named</td>
          <td><code>[[durable_objects.bindings]]</code>, <code>[[migrations]]</code>, a <code>do://SITES/{tenant}</code> connection</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Plain settings the app reads with <code>getenv()</code> go under <code>[vars]</code>;
       secrets go to Cloudflare, never into the file.</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">npx wrangler secret put SOLI_SESSION_SECRET   # 32+ characters</code></pre>
    <p>The app can tell where it runs: <code>getenv("SOLI_RUNTIME")</code> is
       <code>"cloudflare-workers"</code> there.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <h2>Deploy</h2>
<pre><code class="language-bash">soli edge build                  # → dist/edge
cd dist/edge && npx wrangler deploy</code></pre>
    <p>For your own domain, once its zone is on the same Cloudflare account, add to
       <code>wrangler.toml</code>, above the <code>[assets]</code> table:</p>
<pre><code class="language-toml">routes = [{ pattern = "app.example.com", custom_domain = true }]</code></pre>
    <p>A Wrangler API token needs <em>Workers Scripts: Edit</em> on the account, and
       <em>Workers Routes: Edit</em> on the zone for a custom domain. With access to several
       accounts, set <code>account_id</code> in <code>wrangler.toml</code>.</p>
  </li>
</ol>
